**Position Summary**
--------------------

**Join a company where the work you do makes a difference!** We are **One Team** with **One Goal**. At STERIS Applied Sterilization Technologies (AST), it’s our philosophy and our way of doing business. Through a network of over 50 facilities globally, STERIS AST has been committed to providing contract sterilization services to the medical device, pharmaceutical, consumer, and industrial communities for over 40 years. Our irradiation and gas sterilization services ensure the safety of those who use these products, including our families, our friends, and ourselves.

We are seeking an experienced **Quality Assurance Manager**, to lead the Quality function at our **Whitby, ON**, facility. You will play a key role in shaping quality strategy, driving continuous improvement, ensuring regulatory compliance, and building a culture of operational excellence.

As the QA Manager, you will provide strategic leadership for the site's **Quality Management System (QMS)**, ensuring compliance with global regulatory and quality standards while driving a culture of continuous improvement. You will oversee quality systems, regulatory compliance, supplier quality, process quality, and quality improvement initiatives across the Whitby facility. You will partner closely with site leadership to strengthen operational performance, maintain audit readiness, and ensure compliance with standards including ISO 9001, ISO 13485, MDSAP, FDA 21 CFR Part 820/211, and EU MDR.As the site's **Management Representative**, you will champion quality excellence, lead quality strategy, and help ensure STERIS continues to deliver safe, reliable, and compliant services to customers around the world.

Please note that this is an on-site leadership position based in our facility in Whitby, ON, with up to 20% travel.

**What You'll do as a Quality Assurance Manager - QMS & Compliance**
--------------------------------------------------------------------

**Provide Strategic Quality Leadership**

* Lead the site's Quality organization and establish a culture focused on quality, compliance, accountability, and continuous improvement;
* Partner with the Site Leadership Team to align quality objectives with business goals and operational priorities;
* Serve as the site's Management Representative and lead Management Review activities.

**Drive Compliance & Regulatory Excellence**

* Ensure continued compliance with applicable standards and regulations, including: ISO 9001, ISO 13485, MDSAP, FDA 21 CFR Part 820 and Part 211, EU MDR;
* Maintain inspection and audit readiness while supporting successful customer, regulatory, and certification audits;
* Act as the site's Person Responsible for Regulatory Compliance (PRRC) in accordance with EU MDR requirements.

**Advance Continuous Improvement**

* Lead site-wide quality improvement initiatives using data-driven decision making;
* Monitor key performance indicators and implement corrective and preventive actions that improve quality, efficiency, and customer satisfaction;
* Collaborate with Operations and Engineering teams to strengthen process capability and process controls.

**Support Product & Supplier Quality**

* Provide quality leadership throughout product and process development activities;
* Oversee supplier quality programs and risk-based supplier qualification processes;
* Ensure effective complaint investigation and resolution processes that drive meaningful improvements.

**Develop High-Performing Teams**

* Coach, mentor, and develop Quality team members;
* Foster collaboration across Manufacturing, Engineering, Regulatory Affairs, Supply Chain, and Operations functions;
* Build organizational capability through leadership, talent development, and succession planning.

**The Experience, Skills and Abilities Needed**
-----------------------------------------------

*Required*

* Bachelor's degree in Engineering or another relevant technical discipline;
* 8+ years of experience in Quality Systems, Quality Engineering, Manufacturing Quality, or related disciplines within a regulated industry;
* 8+ years of experience working within ISO-certified environments;
* 2+ years of experience leading and developing teams;
* Strong working knowledge of quality systems, risk management, auditing, and regulatory compliance;
* Eligibility to meet EU MDR Article 15 requirements for PRRC responsibilities;
* Demonstrated ability to influence cross-functional stakeholders and drive organizational change;
* Excellent communication, problem-solving, and decision-making skills.

*Preferred*

* Experience in medical devices, healthcare, pharmaceuticals, sterilization, or other highly regulated industries;
* Knowledge of Quality System Regulations (QSR), GMP requirements, and international quality standards;
* Experience with statistical analysis tools, process improvement methodologies and Lean manufacturing environments;
* ASQ certifications are considered an asset.

**What STERIS Offers**
----------------------

This is an opportunity to join a company that will invest in you for the long-term. STERIS wouldn’t be where it is today without our incredible people, who take true pride in their work. That’s why we share in our success together by rewarding employees for their hard work.

*Here is just a brief overview of what we offer:*

* Market Competitive Pay;
* A range of employee benefits, including:
  + A comprehensive and flexible group insurance plan – offering various options and approximately 90% covered by STERIS. This plan includes prescription drug coverage, vision care, paramedical services, and dental care;
  + Telemedicine services;
  + An Employee Assistance Program (EAP);
  + A bank of personal days (5 days);
  + Paid-time off;
  + A day off on your work anniversary;
  + A group RRSP with employer contributions from STERIS, up to 3% of annual salary;
  + A corporate bonus program;
* An experienced and multidisciplinary team;
* A safe environment at the forefront of continuous improvement.
* Excellent opportunities for advancement and stable long-term career.

